  "hypothesis": "Packing the shorter boundary dimension into contiguous strips and advancing four consecutive boundary starts together lets one loaded strip update four rolling sums, reducing source-matrix traffic while preserving cache-resident counting state.",
  "notes": "A bounded locality/blocking experiment: four-start strip blocks are dynamically distributed across at most the four available cores; each worker owns its padded rolling strips and compact generation-tagged frequency table.",
